    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d413">

                <pb facs="0612" n="512" sameAs="frus:frus1934v02/pg512"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">862.002 Hitler, Adolf/34</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Germany</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Dodd</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 600</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Berlin</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1934-03-08">March 8, 1934</date>.<lb/>[Received March
                        17.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Referring to my confidential telegram No.
                    48, of March 6, <hi rendition="#italic">12</hi> noon, I have the honor to
                    enclose herewith copies and translation of the memorandum therein mentioned. It
                    will be noticed that this was not written on stamped paper nor did it bear any
                    initial or signature. <pb facs="0613" n="513" xml:id="pg513"/> There does not
                    seem, therefore, to be any necessity for the Department to make a reply other
                    than that contained in its cable No. 29, of March 6, 1 p.m., the gist of which I
                    shall transmit to the Foreign Office whenever the occasion presents itself.</p>
                <p>If however the Department desires to make some observations in regard to the
                    German propaganda in the United States it seems to me that portions of this
                    memorandum would afford a convenient pretext; I do not in any sense wish to
                    recommend that the Department make a reply, merely to mention the
                    possibilities.</p>
                <p>Respectfully yours,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">William E. Dodd</hi></signed></closer>


                <xi:include href="d413-a1.xml" xpointer="d413-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
